Hi Andrew,
I'd suggest you login on the console as you described and then login via
a terminal also ; check out which of the console's processes are hanging
then
by looking in the output from ps -ef. I have had a similar problem
recently
and found it was the automounter on my system that was hanging the X
display,
as X was using automounter, but not incoming telnet sessions.

You should be able to see the PIDs for you console login and work out
which
ones are hanging by looking at which are the parents and which are the
children and also looking at the process creation time column.

Hope this helps,
Paul

