Not from Compaq/Digital - Digital never did any testing with
processors it didn't sell the PCs with.  I see lots of "turbo" upgrade
chips/modules on the market - it might be a good idea to start with
the makers of those.

I had a CelebrisFP 590 which ran fine with a 166 non-MMX OverDrive
chip.  I heard from many that the MMX version did not work, nor did
faster OverDrive chips (which all had MMX).

Nowadays,  I'd have to ask what the return is for doing this sort of
upgrade and would it perhaps be more cost-effective to simply buy or
put together a new system.  The way prices have fallen and performance
risen, I can't see spending $100-$200 on a faster processor for one of
these boxes.  Turn them into Linux servers or something like that! :-)


