Andrew Gallagher <ab.gallagher@am.qub.ac.uk> writes:

> Morning!
> 
> I have been having trouble for a while with an Alpha workstation running
> DU 4.0E. After a reboot, dtlogin hangs on the local console (X starts,
> no login window appears but all processes seem to be running). Remote X
> terminals are unaffected. In the past, the problem has fixed itself
> after a week or so, but this is hardly satisfactory (lucky it doesn't
> get rebooted often).
> 
> There are no errors reported in /var/dt/Xerrors aside from the usual
> font nonsense (which has probably been created by people working away
> from remote X terminals). Likewise there is little amiss in
> /var/adm/syslog.dated/ .
> 
Did you look at the Xsetup file? By default in /usr/dt/config but if
you copied / created it in /etc/dt/config it will use that instead.
This is where the font path to the CDE fonts is established. The
behaviour you describe is often caused by an inablitity of CDE to
find / load the CDE fonts. The fonts should be in
/usr/dt/config/xfonts/$LANG (or /etc/dt/config/xfonts/$LANG).
If you are using a font server check that the CDE fonts are included
there (/etc/X11/fs/config), and include a line in Xsetup to point
to the font server ($XDIR/xset fp+ tcp/<hostname>:<portnumber>).

-- 
