In article <38dff5c6_1@127.0.0.1>, "Andrew" <arousch@home.com> wrote:

>The DECNIS 500 has a part# DNSBE-BC.  If there is no console cable how do
>you configure this thing?

You configure it using the clearVISN product on your Windows box or the 
various configuration utilities under OpenVMS or Digital Unix (or even the 
older PC-based tool that was around before clearVISN).

The original MPC-1 had a console port hidden under some peelable label (for 
FCC reasons I think). MPC-2 had a DB25 console port and so did MPC-3 (IIRC). 
The MPC-1 port was MMJ (DEC423).

