OK, hardware guys, time to show what you're worth!

As I'm running out of space on an RZ28D, I want to replace it with an
RZ29B-VW.  I have a BA356 expansion box with the 8 bit personality
module, running in single-bus mode, and connected to an ALPHAstation
255/233, which has a narrow controller.  The jumper in the personality 
module is removed, which is what is needed for single-bus operation.  
Also, the box itself has a jumper instead of a terminator, as needed for 
single-bus operation.  (When I convert to dual-bus operation, how 
difficult is it to install the terminator in place of the jumper?  I 
have the documentation, but it doesn't indicate how easy this is.)

Should this work with the RZ29B-VW inside?  I assume that I only need
the 16 bit personality module if I want to connect it to a wide
controller.  Is this correct? 

I have 5 SBBs I would like to put in the BA356: the RZ29B-VW, two
TLZ06-VA DAT drives and two RZ28A-VA disks.  (Actually, only 4 of these,
as there are already 3 internal SCSI devices in the ALPHAstation; when
everything is working properly, I want to convert it to dual-bus mode
and connect the second SCSI bus to a VAXstation 4000 90).  The BA356 has
1 meter of internal SCSI bus length, the ALPHAstation 1.1.  Thus, a
50-cm connecting cable shouldn't make the SCSI bus exceed the limit of 3
meters.  Interestingly, this doesn't work: the RZ29B does not show up
with SH DEV.  (There seem to be no problems with the BA356 or the
RZ29B-VA per se; both are new (and under warranty, but as I didn't buy
them locally, it might be quicker to solve the problem here in the
newsgroup.))  Any of the three types of devices alone is OK.  Any
combination of 2 devices is OK except the RZ29B-VW and a TLZ06-VA
(RZ29B-VW doesn't show up with SH DEV).  Any combination of three
devices is OK unless it includes the RZ29B-VW (RZ29B-VW doesn't show up
with SH DEV).  I haven't yet tested combinations of 4 devices in the
BA356. 

My first thought was that the RZ29B-VW and the TLZ06-VA are somehow 
increasing the SCSI bus length after all.  However, first, this 
shouldn't be the case, as calculated above.  Second, I then did the 
following: I put the RZ29B-VW and one device in the BA356 and two more 
devices in a BA353 pizza box.  Thus, FOUR devices now, plus some extra 
cabling (inside the BA353 itself an extra external cable, certainly 
exceeding 3 meters total now).  IN THIS CONFIGURATION, EVERYTHING WORKS!
