The MMJ-DB25(female) adapter is H8571-A

There is an RJ45-MMJ adapter (H8584-A) but it's the opposite of what you want 
(i.e. plugs into RJ45 socket and presents an MMJ socket ready for a DEC423 
cable).

Many of the DECserver manuals used to have a few pages showing the pinouts of 
the many adapters that were available. I don't happen to have any of those 
manuals to hand but you may be able to find some online docs on the COMPAQ or 
Cabletron websites (the network business was sold to Cabletron). The DECserver 
900 and DECserver 700 manuals would be a good place to start.

If you cannot find what you need, send me mail and I'll dig out a DECserver 
300 manual I have at home: I'm sure it has the pinout of the H8571-A which 
would allow you to build an adapter to go to DB25.

There's always the Hardware Book at 
http://www.sonic.net/~alanwall/hwb/hwb.html which may help.


