You're going down a road that you don't want to go down.  If you
had RP05's or RM03's hooked to this Alphastation (is this even
possible?) maybe you'd use such tools, but you don't want to use
such tools on a modern SCSI drive.

If the drive isn't fscking, then it's either a sick drive or
the drive's SCSI implementation isn't compatible with DU/Tru64's
SCSI implementation.  Who made the drive?  What model number?
Is it supported by DEC with the OS software that you're using?
How big are the partitions?

Tim.



