Don't exactly quote me on this, but if memory serves me well ...

-  Peak bus bandwidth on DSSI is 4MB/s
-  Peak DSSI bandwidth for an HSD05 is 1MB/s
-  Peak DSSI bandwidth for an HSD10/HSD30/HSD50 is 3MB/s
-  Peak bus bandwidth for Narrow SCSI is 5MB/s
-  Peak bus bandwidth for Wide SCSI and/or Fast-Narrow is 10MB/s
-  Peak bus bandwidth for Fast-Wide SCSI is 20MB/s
-  Peak bus bandwidth for UltraSCSI is 40MB/s

You'd also want to look into the Peak IO/sec counts for each of the
controllers involved, but I don't have that handy.  I never worked with FDDI
so can't help there.


