Bill wrote:
> 
> I thought about paint, but not sure if it would look better or worse,
> due to chipping.

 I've had moderate luck using a cleaning product called SoftScrub. It's
a mildly abrasive household cleaning product that also has a small
amount of bleach in it. Applied with a wet sponge and scrubbed VERY
carefully, It takes off some of the top layers of the plastic (like I
say, VERY carefully), and will remove some of the discoloration. If the
color is very bad it won't get it all, but it dramatically improved the
appearance on a LA-120 and other DEC gear I've collected.

  Ron



