OK.  Right after I posted this plea for help I went back over to the PC,
looked in and there semi-staring me in the face was "N/OFF PASSWORD
CLEAR..."  The beginning was obscurred under a plastic clip on either side
of the cache module.  I removed the clip and there it was "J20 ON/OFF
PASSWORD CLEAR...)

I set J20 on, powered on the system, pressed F2 to get into the BIOS and
viola! I was in.  After tinkering in the BIOS and saving my changes I let
the system reset itself and then there was a message "Password cleared.
Remove jumper"  Powered the system off.  Set removed the jumper from J20 and
everything is dandy.

Talk about quick turn around for help.  I asked a question and received the
answer without even receiving a reply!  ;-)

Now if I could only find specs for the mobo so I know what CPU I can swap in
in place of the Intel P100.
Anyone know if this board is MMX capable?  I have an AMD K6-2 266 just dying
to be "put back into the game".

Thanks again,
Jim



