Jim,

Your AMD K6-2 266 will have to continue to be just dying to be "put
back into the game".  I'm pretty sure the GL5100ST is not capable of
even running an MMX CPU.  It all depends on the model of motherboard
in the computer.  What is the DEC part number of the motherboard?  Is
the CPU socket labeled "Socket 5" or "Socket 7".  If the latter, the
system is at least capable of 200MHz.  If Socket 5, the design limit
may be either 100MHz or 133MHz.  In any event, you can install a
Pentium OverDrive CPU (max 200 MHz) or an Intel CPU-based processor
upgrade, either PowerLeap or Kingston.  I've never tried, but I'd be a
little dubious that your computer would run a non-Intel CPU.

... Ben Myers

