"Hans Vlems" <hvlems@iae.nl> writes:
> It was available with a BI interface (TU81) and a STI interface (TA81).

I wrote:
> The TU81 interface is not BI, it is LESI.

"Hans Vlems" <hvlems@iae.nl> writes:
> The LESI acronym (AFAIK) refers to whatevers happens between
> tapedrive and controller.
> I was referring to the bus into which the controller plugs. The BI, the
> UNIBUS (VAX and PDP) had various controllers built for them.

Your explanation isn't consistent; you list a computer bus (BI) for the
TU81 (even though the TU81 does not connect directly to BI), and a
drive interface (STI) for the TA81.

Anyhow, neither the TU81 nor the TA81 will plug into a BI.  Or a
Unibus, Massbus, Qbus, XMI, SBI, Turbochannel, or PCI.  It makes no
more sense to call a TU81 an SBI device than it would to call an TU58
a Unibus device.



