I have one of these PC64 Systems, and the Firmware upgrade
occured without any problem, although I did have one board fail on me.
It just locked up one day as I was using it.
It just did nothing, after that.. 

Curiously,all the voltages were there but the processor
didn't even get warm, so you should check that  !! 
It was exchanged under warranty,
and the replacement has been fine.

You need 36-bit SIMMs in lots of four for this board.
Non-parity wont work.

Serial ports are on the board but you will need the 
cables. Beware there are two common types, 
of pinout and 
of course I had the wrong ones. I made some 
up myself in the end.

You should be able to force the board to come up
 in debug console, by changing a link on the board,
and upgrade firmware from there. Don't bother with
the serial console. I couldn't get this to work
from the ARC bios !

All manuals are avalable on  the Digital web site in PDF form.

Anycase you should see some BIOS messages on the screen
at powerup, even with no disks attached,e etc Perhaps the video card
is faulty.

I haven't much to go on here, but as I say I did have one 
suffer a hard failure..

AJT



