Morning!

I have been having trouble for a while with an Alpha workstation running
DU 4.0E. After a reboot, dtlogin hangs on the local console (X starts,
no login window appears but all processes seem to be running). Remote X
terminals are unaffected. In the past, the problem has fixed itself
after a week or so, but this is hardly satisfactory (lucky it doesn't
get rebooted often).

There are no errors reported in /var/dt/Xerrors aside from the usual
font nonsense (which has probably been created by people working away
from remote X terminals). Likewise there is little amiss in
/var/adm/syslog.dated/ .

