The jumper settings are usually shown on a label on the top of
the disk:-

With the disk held component board down and looking at the
jumpers' end:-

The 3 left-most jumpers set the SCSI address (jumper in = binary
1).

The remaining jumpers read left to right are:-
Fault (not a jumper but a single pin),
Busy,
+5VDC,
Spin Up,
AC Low,
Reserved,
SP Sync.

IIRC there was some discussion recently in this or a related NG
as to when to install the spin up jumper. The others have always
been left off in DEC VAX and ALPHA systems I've ever met.

The 2-page card I have from DEC gives little other useful
information except that it's 1.05Gb formatted (which you knew
already). Email me if you want a posted or FAXed copy.

