Exactly which VAXstation is it?

Does it work at all - i.e. with a monitor?

You have S3 correct; the other one should not matter.
Where have you plugged in the terminal?
IIRC, If there is no good memory, then you get nothing (and the lights freeze 
on a pattern that I cannot remember right now).

>I suspect the problem is either the cable or the VT setup.  Does the 
>cable need to be crossed or not?  Should it go into the port with the 
>picture of the printer, or into the one with the double arrows (I 
>believe the former).  What are the relevant settings in the setup menue?

On both the VAXstation 4000-90 and VAXstation 4000-60 there are two ports (a 
DB25 and an MMJ) each of which has both a double-arrow icon and a printer 
icon. Either of these ports will do - they are the same port IIRC. The DEC423 
should be standard, crossed (unless my eyesight is failing me).

If perchance you have a VLC (never met one in the flesh yet) I *believe* (but 
cannot verify) that you must have a graphics board in for the alternate 
console to work - even though the graphics board will not be used.

Watch the memory in the VS4000-90: it goes in a non-obvious order, read the 
legend carefully! Get it wrong and you'll be scratching your head for a while.

