:I'm using a |d|i|g|i|t|a|l| cable, DEC OPTION NUMBER EO-BC16E-10,  DEC
:PART NUMBER 17-00811-02.  It appears to be crossed, i.e. the order of
:the wires (according to the colours) is at one end compared to the
:other.  I seem to remember one needs a crossed cable, so perhaps the 
:problem is somewhere else.  The terminal is set to 8 bits, no parity, 1 
:stop bit, no local echo, transmit=receive=9600, XOFF at 64, DEC-423, 
:data leads only.

  The BC16E DECconnect wiring always contains a cross-over -- the adapters 
  handle any necessary "reorganization" in the wiring.  (The Bell Labs 
  modular wiring system -- the right-, left-, and center-keyway modular
  jack schemes -- also always contains a cross-over in the cabling.)

  The VAXstation 4000 VLC uses the printer MMJ as the alternate console
  connection, when S3 is switched upward.  Remember to power-cycle the 
  box after changing the console port setting.

  Check the FAQ for the pinouts and the adapters...

