>> The abouve statement worked. I could not find any documentatuib on the
>> dial. I set it to agent and now it boots. I get to image load
>complete,
>> but now i can't type anything using the console port.

Try and error. Like me. Or ask a friend. Like me. ;-)
I already posted this hint some time ago but IIRC this year.

>Everything works now. It takes a long time to boot and i was impatient.

If you boot the compressed image (MNENG2) - eg. because you only have the
1MB Flash RAM variant of the DECserver 90M (DSRVH-MA) or because you
choose to do it anyway (but why ?) or because you didn't know that there
are two different variants (uncompressed is MNENG3) of the boot image
then a loadfile decompression takes place after the boot and before
the server responds to anything.

And this compressions lasts 5min, which is ridicolous/unacceptable and is
one of the reasons why the 1MB flash variant of the DECserver 90M is
no longer produced/sold now. (The 2MB variant is DSRVH-PA)

