> > 4) Keep track of Q-Q and Q-CD slots, so that you don't put a Q-bus card
> >    in a CD slot.
> ??? =:-O

I assume you have read the line pointed out by others, but in short:
Some backplane slots have the Q-bus going like a serpentine;
top->bottom->next slot
but some slots, at the head of the bus just run the Q-bus through the top,
and instead have what is called CD-slots in the bottom half. You cannot
insert Q-bus cards in the CD-slot. Some quad-height cards, however,
require to be in a Q-CD slot.

> > (Nb. CD here isn't a compact disc. :-)
