On Sun, 15 Mar 3900 08:40:02, "Jake" <jdillipl@NOSPAM.concentric.net> 
wrote:

> If you read the original post, this is a SCSI system, not IDE.  Volker, are
> you sure this is a 2940UW and not a 2940U2W?  the U2W requires a different
> driver (aic78u2.sys) from what the 2940UW uses (aic78xx.sys).

> > >Konfiguration: DEC Alpha 21164 + PC164 Board +
> > >Adaptec AHA 2940 UW + IBM DCAS 34330 UW

> > >Stop: 0X0000007B; ... Inaccessable_Boot_Device
> > >

I don't know what size a DCAS 34330 is but I'm not convinced that NT4 
without FP4 is not subject to the bootable 8GB partition limit even 
for scsi devices. However, the most likely cause of this is that the 
wrong scsi driver is being used.

The trick, in all cases, when you see this lovely message is to ensure
that the drivers you need for installation are specified at Install 
time. The bit where it asks for 'extra storage devices'. Get it wrong 
and you have an inaccessible boot device. The correct driver has been 
loaded during install but the wrong one is loaded during boot.

Had this last w/e when changing mother boards  (yeah it was IDE but 
I've had similar where my boot partition was on a SCSI disk.) e.g 
Changing from SYMBIOS-U to TEKRAM-UW. The Repair disk gets you out of 
that mess but you need the required drivers on a diskette.

Cheers - Dave.



