Andrea,

I'm pretty sure that the BIOS of the Celebris XL5133 is old enough
that it won't handle an 8.4GB drive.  Sure sounds that way from your
description.  The Celebris XL and Prioris XL were designed primarily
to use SCSI drives, and it seems to me that IDE was pretty much an
afterthought because the IDE capability was present on the motherboard
chipset.

You might succeed with Linux together with the typical software
provided by the drive manufacturer to deal with BIOS limitations.  Go
to the website of the hard drive manufacturer to download.

Otherwise, you can install a 16-bit add-in card that has a hard disk
BIOS on it.  www.microfirmware.com is one place to start.  Their
BIOS-only card replaces the hard disk BIOS with one that handles all
sorts of IDE drives... Ben Myers

