Bill <s2521@bellatlantic.net> wrote:
> someone use for a replacement?  1-800-DIGITAL isn't working anymore...


It's roughly a 73MB MFM disk.  If replacing it with another MFM disk, I'd
recommend an RD54 which is ~150MB and far more reliable.

OTOH, if you shop around you can probably find a 3rd party ESDI controller
and a ESDI drive for a lot less than the cost of a RD54.  

Of course the best route to take is to find a Q-Bus SCSI card, such as a
VIking or CMD card.

What's the best choice, it really boils down to is this a hobbyist system or
is it used for work (since you mention 1-800-DIGITAL I suspect it's a work
system).  If it's Hobbyist check out the ESDI route, if it's work switch to
SCSI if you can, otherwise getting a RD54 might be the best route.

Actually another good question might be what kind of system do you need this
for.  If it's a PDP-11, the recommendations above are good.  If it's a
MicroVAX, then you might want to look at moving to a slightly more modern
VAX that has built in support for SCSI.

With a better idea of what this is for, I could offer better advice.

			Zane



