My first answer is no.  That's based upon what I view as network activity.

You can use an ethernet based terminal server with terminals connected to the
terminal server.  From there the user can CONNECT to any VMS (and maybe
Unix/Linux) node on the network.  But the connections will still be for
character cell terminals, the same as used on serial ports.  (Actually, what the
terminal server provides is serial ports, which can allow connections to any
node supporting LAT, DECNET, and in some cases TCP/IP.)

