Wolfgang Rupp wrote:
> 
> situation:
> I have a PDP-11/23+ and a MicroVAX II, both full of strange an not so
> strange I/O cards. And I have a DECsystem 5500 with nothing except the
> CPU and DSSI controller, it was a fileserver.
> 
> I'd like to move cards around, but as I understand, it does matter
> what card sits where in the Qbus. Searching the Net did not turn up
> any guide in that direction. Does somebody have a pointer?

Well, it does matter, but perhaps not in the way that you might think.
A few rules:

1) Cards that do DMA and have small buffers should be placed near the CPU.
2) The RQDX1 *must* be last, since the design is faulty.
3) Cards must be placed with no "holes" in the bus.
4) Keep track of Q-Q and Q-CD slots, so that you don't put a Q-bus card
   in a CD slot.

(Nb. CD here isn't a compact disc. :-)

	Johnny

