Unfortunately, I've already discovered a bug and had another one reported:

1) USER_INFO.SAH actually does produce multiple versions.  That was one file
that I missed.

2) Even though the rest of the files do not produce zillions of versions,
their version numbers do increase.  This can cause a problem if you get up
to 32K.

3) The client always sets its priority to 3 even if this is an increase.
(Someone reported this happening from a batch queue with base priority 0).
The workaround is explicitly specify the priority you want with

    -nice n

Sorry about that.  We'll try to do something about them for the next
version.

