Just FYI - Prices for systems which are normally not sold to household 
users generally do not appear in open market literature.  Prices vary by 
contract and source and are quite dynamic, thus you won't find the cost 
for an Alpha indiscriminately posted anywhere. 

If you do find an interest in a couple choices from the various web 
sources such as http://www.compaq.com/buynow/online.html I will be glad to 
look for someone in the company who can price it for you.  

Also let me make you aware that several companies have offered Alphas in 
laptops before, in magnesium alloy cases for durability and heat 
dispersion.  Since some Alphas were made to run at 2.2v it reduced heat 
and battery usage enough to make laptop Alphas practical.  "Tadpole" in 
England and "Alpha Research Technologies" (not DEC or Compaq affiliated) 
in the Midwest have offered Alpha portables in the past. 

You may even find some Alpha desktops at greatly reduced prices at the 
online compaq store (www.compaqfactoryoutlet.com).  I believe they 
sometimes let non-employees buy this new or excess or reconditioned 
hardware.  If you are a military member you can also avail yourself of the 
Desktop contract, which allows DoD members to buy systems for home use at 
the reduced military prices (at least they did in the last contract 
run).   

I wish you luck.  There wasn't anything an Alpha couldn't do best in my 
arena of military intelligence despite SUN worshippers' propaganda, the 
Alpha was chosen as the chip for Cray Supercomputers before SGI bought 
Cray, and Compaq is now putting together Europes most powerful 
supercomputer for the French government.  

CARP 


