I'm not the expert in this area, but I did ask around.
Below is the reply I got:

<quote>
These symbols are from a pre version 6.0 standard library.
If you are not compiling with -oldcxx, they should not
be in any of your objects or libraries. If you look in
/usr/include/cxx you will see they do not exist in
any of the version 6.1 header files, they are only in the headers
in /usr/include/cxx_oldcxx (which gets used if you compile
with -oldcxx).

Did you recompile ALL of your sources with this new compiler?

If you ARE compiling with -oldcxx, then are you using
the command "cxx -oldcxx" to do the link?
</quote>

Let us know if this helps or if you can provide more info.

-Jeff

