People - here's the deal with 50 pin drives

DEC made a multitude of the LED connector that call connected to the
17-03608-01 - I think that's it - the flex cable from the drive to the
outside of the box

Depending on what drive, the flex pins would connect a certain way into the
back of the drive or even the front of the drive

You're all best off just buying the original DEC drive USED - you don't pay
much more than a regular brick drive and you can get them maitained by
DECpaq

Warning - we used to supply the canisters - and we found out the hard way
that IF you put one of your home built drives into a DEC enclosure - YOU
WILL VOID ALL Warranty on the System and Subsystem - serious

