> >> better than the 16 hours or so it takes under VMS on a PWS 500a).
> >
> > Strange, it takes 7.5 hrs under VMS 7.2 on my PWS 500au. (4 MB cache).
> >
>    Could it be the cache size that makes the difference? I'll have to
> check what size cache the PWS500a has. Somehow 2MB comes to mind.
> 
>    Still doesn't explain where the ~1 hour EV6 results are coming from when
> a DS10 takes ~6 hours, under either VMS or Unix. Cache size again?

Cache is very important for Seti. If the the whole program and a lot of
the data fits into cache it will run much faster. For the PWS 500 series
this also applies to benchmark results. With 4MB cache the specfp95
results are much better than with 1MB cache, most likely because the
benchmark program(s) fit better into cache.

For the new 2000 series of benchmarks they have altered the programs in
such a way that the effect of the cache is no longer so prominent, thus
making the results more realistic and also to include the effect of the
rest of the computer and cpu design.



