OK, I'm not a hardware specialist either, but here is what I have been
told.

Unless the StorageWorks cannister itself has address switches, the BA350
sets the address of the drive based on the position in the chassis. 
SCSI ID 0 is the topmost drive with SCSI ID 6 being the one above the
power supply.

I suspect that this is not the problem, though.

The BA350 chassis is a narrow SCSI chassis.  The RZ29B-VW is a wide
drive.  From what I have been told, they will not work together.

You want narrow SCSI cannisters for a BA350.  These normally have a -VA
suffix.

