Take a look at the results by CPU type. Alpha takes ~8 hours, EV6 takes ~1
hour 21 minutes, EV67 takes ~1 hour 1 minute, and an undesignated Alpha
(EV68, mayhap?) takes ~59 minutes to crunch a workload. Based on the CPU
performance figures, one might infer that the OpenVMS results are generated
on older, slower Alpha systems while the T64 results hail from newer iron.

Alpha, of course, trounces all competitors in workload completion speed. A
shame CPQ doesn't leverage this fact.

