> and introduction process needs a good dose of fiber and some exercise!

The 833MHz EV67s have been in use inside Compaq since last August or earlier
(August 16 was the first time I saw such parts). It may well be that CPQ has
elected to eschew production of 833MHz parts and to go directly to ~1GHz.
Given IA-32's imminent achievement of GHz bragging rights, CPQ's approach
might make sense.

On the other hand, the WildFire architecture supports Alphas in speed
increments of ~104MHz. Hence 833MHz makes sense given that the initial WF
CPU bin is ~729MHz.

On a related note, the Samsung/API roadmap called for ~933MHz parts a month
or so ago, and 1GHz parts right about now. Haven't heard--or seen--anything
from these folks, tho'...






