> > Unless the StorageWorks cannister itself has address switches, the BA350
> > sets the address of the drive based on the position in the chassis. 
> > SCSI ID 0 is the topmost drive with SCSI ID 6 being the one above the
> > power supply.
> 
> I've also heard the opposite; which is correct?

The StorageWorks shelves I've worked with have been mounted
in a rack so "topmost" doesn't make sense.  For me, slot 0
has been on the right next to where the cable goes in when
the power is on the left.

You should be able to check things with a "Show dev" at the
SRM (>>>) prompt.  Start with an empty shelf to see what your
system has internally.  Then add a disk and see what device-ID
it gets.  You may have to rrun Init (or power cycle) for the
system to discover a new disk.

