  A relatively early TURBOchannel Alpha box (no PCI)...

  For details, see:

    http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/archive/index.html

  Systems of this vintage have tended to use the older non-PC-compatible
  keyboard and mouse, meaning you have to find a VSXXX-GA and LK401
  keyboard -- see the OpenVMS FAQ and many previous discussions here and
  over in comp.os.vms for details on (the various troubles with) swapping 
  (or trying to swap) PC standard widgets with older Alpha and VAX 
  peripherals -- the interfaces used long predate the prevalence of the
  PC interface "standard"...

  I would (personally) tend to prefer an AlphaStation or later series
  Alpha system, both for the PCI and the keyboard and mouse interface.

  Pricing is limited by the entry-level AlphaServer DS10 box...

  OpenVMS hobbyist licensing information -- OpenVMS operates nicely on
  the DEC 3000 series -- is included in the OpenVMS FAQ.

