I hope I understand the problem correctly:
You have a DECstation with AUI (thickwire) only and a a PC with thinwire
and/or UTP?

The simplest way to do this is to go for a transceiver (Telesys or so).
The transceiver attaches to the 15 pin connector and delivers either UTP or
coax (thin or thick) whatever you like.

Another possibility: buy transceiver cables and a DELNI, which is thick
ethernet in abox.
Most companies will give you the DELNI for free (some might even pay you for
taking it away...)

Hans Vlems

