Darryl,

My first Alpha machine was a 3000/400, which came from auction with no keyboard,
monitor or mouse. Couldn't believe how fast it was when I finally got it going -
had OSF/1 version 1 on the disk. At the time, was using a Vaxstation II GPX and
a 386 pc and the performance improvement was stunning.

You will need a keyboard/mouse lead, LKxxx series keyboard and dec mouse. Also,
a monitor that will work sync on green. Most modern Sony and Diamondtron
multisync will work, but have yet to see a better monitor than the Dec Trinitron
VRT19HA which I finally managed to trade for my machine. All the bits should be
cheap now though. The monitor will be the most expensive, but you may even be
able to find the above mentioned monitor for a few tens of $, or even being
dumped, as they are fixed frequency and useless for wintel boxes. Any lk series
keyboard should work. I used the LK201 from a VT220 terminal.

They will run NetBSD, but am not sure about Turbochannel framebuffer support.
You may have to run via the serial console or remote the X display, but check
the NetBSD website to confirm.

Good solid machine, and built like a brick outhouse, even if not the fastest
now...

Rgrds, Chris
  

