Hello.
I'm the chief of engineer who suppiled below up2000 and 36GB hard disk.
I tested 4 hard disks in the up2000 with onboard SCSI and with Q-Logic
SCSI controller.
Of course we upgraded frimware to support onboard SCSI controller.

At firts, I used 9.1 GB 7200rpm IBM SCSI hard disk. This hard disk is
succefully recognized and
I installed RedHat 6.1 with SRM console in up2000.
The second hard disk is 18GB 7200rpm segate hard disk. Two hard disks
are shown on SRM console.
RedHat6.1 is succefully installed.
The thrid, I connected 18GB 10000rpm segate hard disk. It failed. At
last, 36 GB cheeta failed too.
I think up2000 can't support 10000rpm hard disk.

All hard disks showed same results with Q-Logic SCSI controller.
In the Alpha Bios, the same.

All hard disks are succefully connected in the compaq DS10 and DS20.

I will test 36GB 7200rpm baracuda harddisk in the up2000. If it will
success, i will conclude that up2000 can't support 10000rpm SCSI hard
disks!

If API's engineer can see this messages, I hope to see API's official
apply.
In Korea, Samsung supply up2000 and alpha CPU's. But I can't get any
informations about up's from Samsung. Sometimes we give technical
information to Samsung.
I can't believe that Samsung is making Alpha CPU's!

If I can't get any reliable information about up2000 from API or
Samsung, we will give up to sell up2000 or any up series Alpha systems
in Korea.


P.S. We showed PowerRAC320 to Samsung Alpha Team. They didn't know the
