  Some background: this Ethernet LAN (re)configuration has little to do 
  with the particular host system and is generally entirely transparent 
  to the host system.  (This deliberately ignores any discussions of the
  host communications software requirements.)

  Yes, there are Ethernet widgets (repeaters) which can get you from a
  ThickWire or ThinWire Ethernet LAN over to a twisted pair LAN.  The
  easiest way here would likely involve a DESTA or similar to get from 
  the AUI connection on the DECstation 5000 MIPS Ultrix box over to a
  ThinWire segment, a couple of T-connectors, some lengths of coax, a
  pair of terminators, and an Ethernet repeater to get from ThinWire 
  over to twisted pair.

  There may well be other approaches available, of course.

